@startuml
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam nodesep 50
skinparam ranksep 60
skinparam dpi 300
skinparam arrowThickness 1.5

title RNN/LSTM Training Process Flow\n(Generic Pipeline for Empathy Prediction Models)

|Data Preparation|
start
:Load Raw Data;
note right
  - Video frames (raw_face)
  - Audio features (speech)
  - Facial landmarks (landmarks)
  - Text transcripts (transcript)
end note

:Extract Features per Modality;
note right
  **Feature Extraction:**
  • Raw Face: Image sequences
  • Speech: Mel spectrograms
  • Landmarks: 68 facial points
  • Transcript: Word embeddings
end note

:Create Sequences with Sliding Window;
note right
  **Windowing Parameters:**
  • seq_len/window_size: 10-100 frames
  • stride: 1-50 frames
  • Captures temporal context
end note

:Load Annotation Labels (Valence);
note right
  **Labels:**
  • Continuous values [-1, 1]
  • Per-frame annotations
  • From Subject_{n}_Story_{m}.csv
end note

:Split into Train/Validation Sets;
note right
  **Typical Split:**
  • Train: Stories 1, 4, 5, 8
  • Validation: Story 2
  • Subjects: 1-10
end note

|Model Definition|
:Define Model Architecture;
note right
  **Architecture Options:**
  1. LSTM with Attention
  2. Bidirectional GRU
  3. Conv3D + Dense
  4. Conv1D + LSTM
end note

:Add Auxiliary Inputs (Optional);
note right
  **Auxiliary Data:**
  • Subject ID embeddings
  • Metadata vectors
  • Late fusion strategy
end note

:Compile Model with CCC Loss;
note right
  **Loss Function:**
  CCC (Concordance Correlation Coefficient)
  loss = 1 - CCC
  
  **Optimizer:**
  Adam (lr=0.0001)
end note

|Training Loop|
:Initialize Callbacks;
note right
  **Callbacks:**
  • ModelCheckpoint (save best)
  • EarlyStopping (patience=5-20)
  • TensorBoard (logging)
  • Metrics (custom CCC tracking)
end note

:Create Data Generators;
note right
  **Generator Benefits:**
  • Memory efficient
  • On-the-fly augmentation
  • Random sampling per epoch
  • Batch generation
end note

repeat :Start New Epoch;

  repeat
    :Generate Training Batch;
    note right
      **Batch Creation:**
      • Random sequence indices
      • Shape: [batch_size, seq_len, features]
      • Corresponding labels
    end note
    
    :Forward Pass;
    note right
      Input → RNN layers → Dense layers → Output
      Output shape: [batch_size, 1]
    end note
    
    :Calculate CCC Loss;
    note right
      **CCC Formula:**
      ρ = Pearson correlation
      CCC = 2ρσ_y σ_ŷ / (σ_y² + σ_ŷ² + (μ_y - μ_ŷ)²)
    end note
    
    :Backward Pass (Backpropagation);
    note right
      • Compute gradients
      • Update weights via Adam
      • Apply dropout regularization
    end note
    
    :Update Model Weights;
    
  repeat while (more batches in epoch?) is (yes)
  ->no;

  :Epoch Complete;

  |Validation|
  :Run Validation;
  note right
    **Validation Process:**
    • No gradient updates
    • Full validation set
    • Calculate val_loss
  end note

  :Calculate Validation CCC;
  note right
    **Metrics Callback:**
    • Predict on validation data
    • Compute CCC and Pearson ρ
    • Print: "ccc = X, pearson = Y"
  end note

  if (Best model so far?) then (yes)
    :Save Model Checkpoint;
    note right
      Save to:
      • best_model.h5
      • Or timestamped file
    end note
  else (no)
  endif

  if (Early stopping criteria met?) then (yes)
    break
  else (no)
  endif

repeat while (more epochs?) is (yes)
->no;

|Post-Training|
:Load Best Model Weights;

:Generate Predictions on Test Set;

:Apply Post-Processing (Optional);
note right
  **Tricks:**
  • Normalize predictions
  • Match train statistics
  • Smooth predictions
  • Median filtering
end note

:Calculate Final Metrics;
note right
  **Final Evaluation:**
  • CCC on test set
  • Pearson correlation
  • Per-subject analysis
end note

:Save Predictions & Results;
note right
  **Outputs:**
  • Prediction CSV files
  • Training history plots
  • Model architecture diagram
  • Performance metrics
end note

stop

legend right
  |= Symbol |= Meaning |
  | Rectangle | Process/Action |
  | Diamond | Decision Point |
  | Note | Additional Info |
endlegend

@enduml

